From: Go08er <149829787+Go08er@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: share immediate latest-target seeking between both APIs

Follow the original -4 immediate/next_seek shape and the maintainer's
September 22 decision. Remove the playing +/-3 s, previous-source +/-2 s,
post-load zero rules and the 250 ms deferred timer machinery. Both APIs now
use the existing non-Ex helper; retain its in-flight latest-target coalescing,
seekability checks, preroll reset, paused target storage and terminal EOF path.

P14 returned success without seek events for all eight isolated playing Ex
requests; the matched ordinary-API control landed all eight.
Retain the old Ex topology-readiness guard in the shared helper, so source
replacement cannot send a premature seek to the outgoing topology. This is
not a time/distance suppression on a ready source. No new debouncer or retry. Burst, sync correction,
source replacement and paused-then-Play still require compiled runtime tests.

